$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of tetrachlorocyclopentadienone
hydrazone (3; R1 = R2 = H; 10.0 g, 0.043 mol) and acid anhydride (0.043
mol) in dry tetrahydrofuran (250 ml) is stirred at room temperature for
0.25-2.0 h. For cyclic anhydrides, triethylamine (4.5 g, 0.043 mol) is
included. Evaporation of tetrahydrofuran, and, where necessary.
extraction with aqueous 20%, hydrochloric acid (100 ml), provides the
crude N-acyl substituted hydrazone 5 which is crystallized from methanol.
N-Acyl Substituted Tetrachlorocyclopentadienone Hydrazones 5. Retention
time 1.0h, Yield 89%. melting point 138-140°C, molecular formula
C7H4Cl4N2O (272.9), microanalysis C ± 0.26, H ± 0.18.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of N-acyl substituted tetrachlorocyclopentadienone hydrazones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Dixon, D. D.; Ford, M. E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1980), (4), 306-8

