$DATUM 38465-60-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Acetoxynaphthalene; Typical Procedure.
2-Naphthol (1; 360 mg, 2.5 mmol) was treated with Ac2O (0.24 mL, 2.5
mmol) under neat conditions at r.t. for 15 min (monitored by GC-MS) under
magnetic stirring in the presence of Cu(BF4)2·xH2O (5.92 mg, 0.025 mmol,
1 mol%). The reaction mixture was diluted with H2O (25 mL) and extracted
with Et2O (3 × 15 mL). The combined ethereal extracts were washed
successively with 2% aq NaOH (15 mL), brine (15 mL), dried (NaSO4) and
concentrated to afford the product, which was in full agreement with the
spectral data (mp, IR, 1H NMR and EIMS) of an authentic sample of
2-acetoxynaphthalene. This typical procedure was followed for the
acetylation of other substrates except that in case of alcohols the
alkali washing was avoided and for amines the alkali washing was replaced
by washing with 1 N HCl. In most of the cases the products gave
satisfactorily spectral (IR, 1H NMR and MS) data without any further
purification. Wherever applicable, purification was performed through
crystallization (for solid) or passing through a column of silica gel
(for liquid) and eluting with 5% Et2O in hexane (Table 3). Yield 89%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
