$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure G. Reaction of amine compounds with acylating agents.
Amine (1 equiv.) was purged with argon, dissolved in pyridine (0.2 M),
and cooled to 0 °C. Acylating agent (1 equiv.) was added, and the
reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 3 h. Saturated NaHCO3 was added,
and the reaction mixture was extracted with 4 x 5 mL of DCM. The combined
organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
Compounds were purified using basic or acidic conditions via preparative
chromatography. Lactam 46a{1}. The compound was prepared according to
general procedure G using 26a (35.0 mg, 0.096 mmol) and acetic anhydride
(0.01 mL, 0.096 mmol). The desired product was isolated as an amorphous
white solid (34.3 mg, 88%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.80 (s, 1H), 7.52
(d, J = 8.4, 1H), 7.21 (d, J = 3.1, 3H), 6.93 (s, 2H), 6.60 (d, J = 8.4,
1H), 6.52 (s, 1H), 4.98 (s, 1H), 3.73 (dd, J = 9.9, 13.6, 1H), 3.16 (s,
3H), 2.98 (d, J = 16.8, 1H), 2.67 (d, J = 16.7, 1H), 2.63 (dd, J = 5.2,
13.6, 1H), 2.10 (s, 3H), 1.86 (s, 1H), 1.00 (d, J = 6.6, 3H), 0.85 (d, J
= 6.6, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 177.7, 173.6, 168.5, 139.6, 134.6,
133.5, 129.0, 128.8, 128.7, 127.7, 121.0, 117.8, 108.2, 69.1, 53.1, 49.1,
40.3, 26.7, 26.6, 24.5, 20.7, 20.1; IR 1674, 2242, 2952, 3293 cm-1; TLC
(EtOAc) RF = 0.09; HRMS (ESI) m / z calcd for C24H27N3O3 (M + H)+
406.2125, found 406.2123.
