$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure G. Reaction of amine
compounds with acylating agents. Amine (1 equiv.) was purged with argon,
dissolved in pyridine (0.2 M), and cooled to 0 °C. Acylating agent (1
equiv.) was added, and the reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 3 h.
Saturated NaHCO3 was added, and the reaction mixture was extracted with 4
x 5 mL of DCM. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. Compounds were purified using basic or acidic
conditions via preparative chromatography. Lactam 46b{1}. The compound
was prepared according to general procedure G using 26b (34.0 mg, 0.094
mmol) and acetic anhydride (0.01 mL, 0.094 mmol). The desired product was
isolated as a pink solid (33.4 mg, 88%). mp 277.0-288.0 °C; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.87 (s, 1H), 7.66 (s, 1H), 7.48 (d, J = 8.4, 1H), 7.26 (m,
3H), 6.96 (s, 2H), 6.67 (d, J = 8.4, 1H), 4.83 (s, 1H), 3.69 (dd, J =
9.4, 13.7, 1H), 3.06 (d, J = 16.9, 1H), 2.83 (s, 3H), 2.77 (d, J = 16.9,
1H), 2.62 (dd, J = 5.6, 13.8, 1H), 2.22 (s, 3H), 1.80 (m, 1H), 0.93 (d, J
= 6.6, 3H), 0.82 (d, J = 6.6, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 175.5,
173.6, 168.8, 139.9, 134.1, 133.8, 132.3, 129.0, 128.4, 127.7, 121.1,
115.4, 108.5, 71.9, 53.3, 49.0, 39.5, 26.5, 26.3, 24.7, 20.8, 20.5; IR
1692, 1701, 1711 cm-1; TLC (EtOAc) RF = 0.11; HRMS (ESI) m / z calcd for
C24H27N3O3 (M + H)+ 406.2125, found 406.2123.
