$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Acetylation Acetic anhydride (0.20 mL, 2.2
mmol) was added to a solution of 2-amino-2-methylpropan-1-ol (0.18 g, 2.0
mmol) in 4 mL of EtOAc. The resulting mixture was stirred, under
nitrogen, for 18 h. Anhydrous potassium carbonate (0.55 g, 4.0 mmol) was
added, and stirring was continued for few minutes (method B). The
reaction mixture was then filtered through a celite path and the filtrate
was concentrated. N-(2-Hydroxy-1,1-dimethyl)acetamide[3b] was obtained in
98% isolated yield (Table 1, entry 14). Table 1. Entry 9, yield 88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
