$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure: A mixture of phthalic
anhydride (1.48 g, 10 mmol) and formamide (1.36g, 30 mmol) was introduced
in a 100-mL flask fitted with a water condenser out of the cavity through
an adaptor and then subjected to microwave irradiation (400 W) for 2 min.
After completion of the reaction, 10 mL of hot water was added and the
crude product was separated by filtration. The solid thus obtained
recrystallized from ethanol to give 1.43 g (97% yield) of phthalimide as
colorless needles. Table: Entry 6, yield 87%. M.P. (°C) Obs, Lit.:
299-300, 30014
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Imidation of cyclic carboxylic anhydrides under microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Peng, Yanqing; Song, Gonghua; Qian, Xuhong
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2001), 31(12), 1927-1931

