$DATUM B. A solution of amine 1a-d (0.020 mol) and maleic anhydride (2.24 g,
0.023 mol) in benzene (100 ml) was heated at reflux for 10 h to give pure
carboxylic acids 2a.
(3aS*,6R*,7S*,7aR*)-2-(Furylmethyl)-1-oxo-1,2,3,6,7,7a-hexahydro-3a,6-epoxyisoindole-7-carboxylic
Acid (2a); Colorless crystals, yield 87%. Empirical formula: C14H13NO5;
Found, %: C, 61.38; H, 4.50; N, 5.64; Calculated, %: C, 61.09; H, 4.76;
N, 5.09; Mp: 150-151°CС; IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1663 (NCO), 1741 (СО2Н);
1Н NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 2.52 (1Н, d, J = 9.3, Н); 2.79 (1Н, d, J
= 9.3, Н; 3.58 (1Н, d, J = 11.2) and 3.94 (1Н, d, J = 11.2, 3-CН2); 4.30
(1Н, d, J = 15.6) and 4.52 (1Н, d, J = 15.6, 2-CH2); 4.99 (1Н, d, J =
1.5, Н; 6.31 (1Н, br. d, J = 3.2, Н); 6.39 (1Н, dd, J = 1.9, J = 3.2, Н);
6.41 (1Н, dd, J = 1.5, J = 5.6, Н; 6.55 (1Н, d, J = 5.6, Н; 7.56 (1Н, br.
d, J = 1.9, Н); 12.11 (1Н, br. s, CO2H); 13C NMR, δ, ppm: 38.8 (СH2);
44.5 (Са); 47.8 (C-3); 49.9 (C-7); 81.1 (C-6); 88.2 (C-3a); 107.8 (C-4');
110.5 (C-3'); 135.5 (C-5); 136.6 (C-4); 142.6 (C-5'); 150.0 (C-2'); 170.1
(C-1); 172.7 (CO2H); MS m/z (Irel, %): 275 [М]+ (3), 231 (2), 194 (47),
176 (31), 150 (18), 121 (12), 109 (64), 99 (61), 80 (100), 69 (24), 54
(94), 43 (63).
