$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B. A solution of amine 1a-d (0.020 mol) and
maleic anhydride (2.24 g, 0.023 mol) in benzene (100 ml) was heated at
reflux for 10 h to give pure carboxylic acids 2a.
(3aS*,6R*,7S*,7aR*)-2-[(5-Methyl-2-furyl)methyl]-1-oxo-1,2,5,6,7,7a-hexahydro-3a,6-epoxyisoindole-7-carboxylic
Acid (2bA); Colorless crystals, yield 86%. Empirical formula: C15H15NO5;
Found, %: C, 62.44; H, 5.07; N, 4.59; Calculated, %: C, 62.28; H, 5.23;
N, 4.84; Mp: 106-108°CС; IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1675 (NCO), 1744 (СО2Н);
1Н NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 2.22 (3H, s, СН3); 2.52 (1Н, d, J = 9.2,
Н); 2.79 (1Н, d, J = 9.2, Н; 3.56 (1Н, d, J = 11.5) and 3.94 (1Н, d, J =
11.5, 3-CН2); 4.20 (1Н, d, J = 15.6) and 4.45 (1Н, d, J = 15.6, 2-CH2);
4.97 (1Н, d, J = 1.7, Н; 5.99 (1Н, dq, J = 0.7, J = 3.0, Н); 6.18 (1Н,
br. d, J = 3.0, Н); 6.41 (1Н, dd, J = 1.7, J = 5.7, Н; 6.55 (1Н, d, J =
5.7, Н; 13C NMR, δ, ppm: 13.3 (CH3); 38.9 (СH2); 44.6 (Са); 47.8 (C-3);
50.1 (C-7); 81.2 (C-6); 88.3 (C-3a); 106.5 (C-4'); 108.8 (C-3'); 135.6
(C-5); 136.7 (C-4); 148.2 (C-5'); 151.3 (C-2'); 170.1 (C-1); 172.8
(CO2H); MS m/z (Irel, %): 289 [М]+ (22), 208 (87), 194 (54), 164 (13),
150 (21), 110 (100), 96 (83), 80 (92), 67 (13), 55 (70), 43 (40).
