$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of N3-Acetylated DHPM 5Aa. A mixture of 1.00 mmol (260 mg) of
DHPM 4A, 2.5 mmol (255 mg, 236 μL, 2.5 equiv.) of acetic anhydride, 2.5
mmol (348 μL, 2.5 equiv.) of TEA, 0.2 mmol DMAP (24 mg, 0.2 equiv.) and
2.0 mL of anhydrous MeCN was irradiated under microwave conditions at 130
°C for 10 min in a 5 mL (large) microwave process vial. To the clear
solution 200 μL of H2O was added, and the reaction mixture was
subsequently irradiated for an additional 5 min at 100 °C. The solution
was filtered through a short plug (1 cm) of silica with an additional
amount of 5 mL MeCN. The filtrate was evaporated and the remaining solid
product treated with Et2O. Yield 254 mg, 84%. >99% purity (HPLC) product,
mp = 169-170 °C (ref. mp = 175-176 °C12). 1H NMR (DMSO-d6): δ 1.17 (t, J
= 7.0 Hz, 3H), 2.30 (s, 3H), 2.43 (s, 3H), 4.08-4.14 (m, 2H), 6.46 (s,
1H), 7.18 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.25-7.34 (m, 3H), 10.20 (br s, 1H); MS
(pos. APCI): m/z 303 (M+1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-assisted scavenging of electrophiles utilizing
polymer-supported sequestration reagents. Application to the synthesis of
N3-acylated dihydropyrimidine libraries
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Dallinger, Doris; Gorobets, Nikolay Yu.; Kappe, C. Oliver
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Molecular Diversity (2003), 7(2-4), 229-245

